@host = http://localhost:5225

### Sign in. Development credentials, seeded by DevelopmentCredentialSeeder.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dev@regos.local",
  "password": "development-password"
}

### Who am I? The first endpoint in RegOS that requires authentication.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### No token at all -> 401, WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### An unsigned token -> 401. Nothing about it is trusted.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.token

### Every failed sign-in returns one status and one message (ADR-022).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dev@regos.local",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### ...including for an address that does not exist.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@regos.local",
  "password": "development-password"
}
